ne10.md story-wiki/Outline.md"]], "output": "```console\n1c1\n< # Outline (rev 10) — one SHAP run per instance: when is it a reliable basis for the conclusion?\n---\n> # Outline (rev 11) — one SHAP run per instance: when is it a reliable basis for the conclusion?\n88c88\n<   - **Floor b by B (K=10 independent backgrounds, same instances as floor a; `floor_b_by_background.csv`):** median top-3 agreement B20 0.46, B50 0.61, B200 0.75, k-means-50 0.77 over 18 cells (rev 9: current CSV, with GMSC MLP; the 0.62/0.72 I quoted in rev 8 were from the earlier delivery). So the background-draw part shrinks with B, as idea-review expected, and a part of the reference's instability (the choice of reference distribution: k-means-50 is not above B200 only by chance: reference-distribution choice is a separate entry) remains. Against the shap default at the default budget floor b is below floor a in 24 of 24 rows (68 of 68 largest-sampled rows), but **against paired Kernel at the same budget the sign is mixed** (13 of 24 rows positive, 7 with CI above 0 at the earlier delivery; with GMSC MLP, 7 of 13 non-linear cells exclude zero, 5 background floor higher, 2 lower). The co-headline is therefore stated for *shap's default estimator at B=50*, with the B curve; \"the value function, not the run, dominates\" is not stated for paired Kernel SHAP or as a general claim. Pending rows: German/ACS-Employment/GMSC MLP (n=10, K=6) are absent, and the run-level share P_c ≥ 0.9 at default is background-invariant (1.0 under every background).\n---\n>   - **Floor b by B (K independent backgrounds, same instances as floor a; `floor_b_by_background.csv`; rev 11: all 20 model × dataset cells delivered, no pending rows):** median top-3 agreement B20 0.45, B50 0.59, B200 0.75, k-means-50 0.77. So the background-draw part shrinks with B, and a part of the reference's instability (the choice of reference distribution; k-means-50 is not above B200 only by chance) remains. Against the headline setting (`shap_kernel`, `l1_reg=False`) at the default budget the paired difference floor b − floor a is negative in all 32 default-budget (d ≥ 16) rows and all 80 largest-sampled rows, CI below 0 in 30 of 32 and 78 of 80; the two exceptions in both are ACS-Employment MLP with k-means-50 and German MLP with B200, the cells with n = 10, K = 6. **Against `kernel_paired` at the same budget the sign is mixed:** positive in 18 of 32 default rows (CI above 0 in 10, below 0 in 8) and 41 of 80 largest-sampled rows (33 above, 35 below). The co-headline is therefore stated for the headline setting at B=50, with the B curve; \"the value function, not the run, dominates\" is not stated for paired Kernel SHAP or as a general claim. The run-level share P_c ≥ 0.9 at default is background-invariant (1.0 under every background).\n108a109\n> - rev 11: floor-b-by-B block refreshed to the 20-cell delivery (b51b17e): medians 0.45/0.59/0.75/0.77; paired difference counts per estimator; no pending rows (experiment-repo, story-repo#7).\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "fe4d50fe-b5ca-5629-b667-b0167cd901dc", "at": 1795655585.5568156, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 97377, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0a40bc7f4b3296b4fb45eaa59cbcdb9e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "8416e3d7-01ec-5a93-b82f-b95a966b934c", "at": 1795655585.5622337, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 97378, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0a40bc7f4b3296b4fb45eaa59cbcdb9e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "1e2d14c5-1991-5b90-bf38-2717